.TH FS80HCTL 1 "March 2026" "fs80hctl 0.1.0" "fs80hctl User Manual"
.SH NAME
fs80hctl \- Technical acquisition, custody, and processing utility for Futronic FS80/FS80H scanners
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fs80hctl
[\fB\-\-json\fR]
.I COMMAND
[\fIARGUMENTS...\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B fs80hctl
is a pure-Rust command-line tool for technical and forensic operations on
Futronic optical fingerprint scanners (FS80, FS80H, and FS81H). It provides direct
optical sensor acquisition, biometric standard compliance (500 DPI), image quality metrics,
format transcoding with immutable chain of custody, and deterministic 1:1 biometric comparison.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
Output results in structured JSON format.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help information and syntax.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print installed program version.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B doctor
Run environment diagnostics (USB subsystem, device permissions, and filesystem write).
.TP
.B devices
List connected Futronic fingerprint scanners on the USB bus.
.TP
.B device inspect [\-\-bus N] [\-\-address N]
Open and inspect USB communication with the specified scanner.
.TP
.B capture [\-o FILE] [\-\-format FORMAT] [\-\-raw] [\-\-wait] [\-\-timeout SECS] [\-\-min\-quality SCORE]
Acquire an optical biometric frame (320x480, 500 DPI) and write the custody manifest (.meta.json). Use \-\-wait for auto-trigger when the finger contact stabilizes.
.TP
.B enroll [\-o FILE] [\-\-samples N] [\-\-timeout SECS] [\-\-min\-quality SCORE]
Acquire multiple samples consecutively and automatically elect and save the highest quality sample (best-of-N).
.TP
.B convert INPUT [\-t FORMAT] [\-o OUTPUT] [\-\-invert]
Transcode across formats (PNG, TIFF, PGM, RAW) while preserving chain of custody.
.TP
.B inspect IMAGE
Inspect metadata, SHA-256 hash, and quality metrics of a biometric image.
.TP
.B verify PROBE [REFERENCE] [\-\-gallery DIR] [\-\-threshold T] [\-\-exit\-code]
Compare biometric images (1:1 with reference file or 1:N against a gallery directory) and calculate technical similarity score.
.TP
.B manual
Display technical reference manual and usage guide on standard output.
.SH SUPPORTED FORMATS
.TP
.B PNG
8-bit grayscale with calibrated pHYs chunk at 500 DPI.
.TP
.B TIFF
Baseline 6.0 with full EXIF tags and 500 DPI resolution.
.TP
.B PGM
Netpbm binary format P5 (NIST NBIS standard).
.TP
.B RAW
Uncompressed 153,600-byte raw pixel dump.
.SH EXIT CODES
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Operational failure or verification threshold not met (when \-\-exit\-code is passed).
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command-line syntax or arguments.
.SH SEE ALSO
docs/MANUAL.md, README.md
